umento_de_diogo_gomes","areaId":"cape_verde","name":"Monumento de Diogo Gomes","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":14.9159,"lng":-23.5096},"visitMinutes":30,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"cape_verde_monumento_de_diogo_gomes","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":5,"wikiPageviews":180,"wikidataSitelinks":3,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13"},"hashtags":["monumentodediogogomes","capeverde"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"The Monumento de Diogo Gomes is a statue at the south end of the Plateau, the historic centre of Praia, on the island of Santiago, Cape Verde. It represents Diogo Gomes, the Portuguese navigator who was one of the discoverers of the island of Santiago in 1460.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Monumento de Diogo Gomes","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/CV-praia-gomez.jpg/1280px-CV-praia-gomez.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/CV-praia-gomez.jpg/500px-CV-praia-gomez.jpg","w":1200,"h":1800,"author":"Balou46","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CV-praia-gomez.jpg"}},{"id":"cape_verde_serra_malagueta","areaId":"cape_verde","name":"Serra Malagueta","category":"viewpoint","tags":["mountains","views","hiking"],"location":{"lat":15.17917,"lng":-23.68333},"visitMinutes":180,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"cape_verde_serra_malagueta","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":102,"wikidataSitelinks":16,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-13"},"hashtags":["serramalagueta","capeverde"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Serra Malagueta is a mountain range located in the northern part of the island of Santiago, Cape Verde. At 1064m elevation, it is the highest point of northern Santiago. The mountain range is protected as the Serra Malagueta Natural Park, which was established on February 24, 2005, and covers 774 hectares.","summaryS